# Planned on bare metal on a 6800U (G3ZIL's home Beelink, RAC 142, Ubuntu
# 24.04.5, libfftw3 3.3.10-1ubuntu3), laid out the way sigmond runs radiod:
# radiod's pair = CPUs 14-15 at 3200 MHz, every other CPU capped at 1400 MHz,
# resctrl group 'radiod' = CPUs 14-15 with L3:0=3ff (10 of 16 ways), xhci
# IRQs moved to 0-13, WD/radiod/decoders stopped, load 0.27 at the start.
# radiod_l3_bytes is the L3 domain sysfs reports (radiod_placement()), not
# the CAT share.  `taskset -c 14 fftwf-wisdom -v -T 1 -n` (fresh, nothing
# imported) over 156 specs: every one of sigmond's 151 FFT_WISDOM_PROFILES
# plus WD's extras.  842 plans; 2 h 6 m 35 s (2026-11-19 18:15Z - 20:21Z).
